# Scanner and detection contract

- `core` owns DNS, TCP 16–20 KB, Telegram, and TLS scanning behavior; command-line prompting and presentation live in `cli`, because scanning must remain usable independently of console interaction.
- Shared configuration, file, network, and error-classification support lives in `utils`, because reusable infrastructure has a separate ownership boundary.
- The configured target lists and runtime settings remain repository-rooted inputs described in `README.md`, because users may override them when running the tool.
